# Plan: Update SunHat to iOS 26.4

## Summary
Update the SunHat app from iOS 26.0 to iOS 26.4, adopting Xcode 26.4 / Swift 6.2 toolchain changes and cleaning up code that targeted iOS 26.0 as a minimum.

---

## Phase 1: Project Configuration Updates

### 1.1 — Bump deployment target to iOS 26.4
- Update `IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET` from `26.0` → `26.4` in `project.pbxproj` (all 6 occurrences across app, test, and UI test targets)
- Update `SWIFT_VERSION` from `6.0` → `6.2`

### 1.2 — Adopt Swift 6.2 Approachable Concurrency build settings
Swift 6.2 (shipped with Xcode 26.4) introduces "approachable concurrency" with these key changes:
- **`defaultIsolation = MainActor`** — the project already sets `SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor`, so this aligns. Verify the setting name hasn't changed in Xcode 26.4.
- **`nonisolated(nonsending)` by default (SE-461)** — nonisolated async functions now run on the caller's actor by default. Audit `nonisolated` usage (currently in `WeatherAPI.swift`, `LocationPermissionManager.swift`) to ensure no behavioral changes.
- **`@concurrent` attribute** — new opt-in for explicit parallelism. No immediate changes needed, but we can adopt it where we want guaranteed background execution.
- **Inferred isolated conformances (SE-470)** — protocol conformances can now be inferred within actor isolation. May simplify some `@MainActor` boilerplate.

### 1.3 — Update CLAUDE.md and migration docs
- Update iOS target references from 26.0 → 26.4
- Update Swift version references from 6.0 → 6.2
- Update Xcode version references
- Update test commands (simulator name/OS version)

---

## Phase 2: Remove Unnecessary Availability Checks

Since the minimum deployment target will be iOS 26.4, all `@available(iOS 26, *)` and `if #available(iOS 26.0, *)` checks are redundant.

### 2.1 — WeatherAPI.swift (lines 44, 55)
- Remove `@available(iOS 26, *)` from `fetchExtendedWeatherData(for:)` and `mapEnhancedCurrentWeather(_:at:)`
- These are now always available

### 2.2 — LocationPermissionManager.swift (line 107)
- Remove `@available(iOS 26, *)` from `requestTemporaryFullAccuracyIfNeeded(purposeKey:)`

### 2.3 — ComprehensiveReminderCreationViewModel.swift (lines 712, 748)
- Remove `if #available(iOS 26.0, *)` checks for MapKit APIs
- Remove fallback branches (dead code with 26.4 minimum)

### 2.4 — SettingsViewModel.swift (line 292)
- Remove `if #available(iOS 18.0, *)` check for `AppStore.requestReview(in:)`
- Remove fallback to `SKStoreReviewController.requestReview()` — iOS 26.4 always has iOS 18+ APIs
- Can also remove `import StoreKit` if `SKStoreReviewController` was the only reason for it (check)

---

## Phase 3: Adopt BGContinuedProcessingTask (New iOS 26 Background API)

iOS 26 introduced `BGContinuedProcessingTask` for user-initiated long-running background tasks with progress reporting and system UI.

### 3.1 — Evaluate adoption in BackgroundWeatherManager
- The current implementation uses `BGAppRefreshTask` for periodic 15-minute weather refresh — this is still correct for automatic background refresh
- `BGContinuedProcessingTask` is better suited for **user-initiated** operations like bulk weather data export or manual "refresh all locations" — consider adding it for explicit user-triggered refreshes
- Add task identifier to Info.plist `BGTaskSchedulerPermittedIdentifiers` if adopting

### 3.2 — Add progress reporting for user-initiated refresh
- When user taps "refresh" in the UI, use `BGContinuedProcessingTask` with progress reporting
- This gives users visibility into background weather fetches via system UI

---

## Phase 4: Swift 6.2 Concurrency Cleanup

### 4.1 — Audit `nonisolated` usage
With SE-461 (`nonisolated(nonsending)` by default), nonisolated async functions now run on the caller's actor. Review:
- `WeatherAPI.swift` — `nonisolated var isAvailable: Bool { get async }` — behavior may change
- `LocationPermissionManager.swift` — `nonisolated` delegate methods — these are sync so unaffected
- Any other `nonisolated` async patterns across ViewModels

### 4.2 — Simplify `@MainActor` annotations
With `SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor` and Swift 6.2 improvements:
- Review which explicit `@MainActor` annotations are now redundant (module-level default makes them unnecessary in many cases)
- Keep `@MainActor` on public API boundaries for clarity

### 4.3 — Adopt `@concurrent` where appropriate
For functions that genuinely need background execution (weather fetching, data processing):
- Mark with `@concurrent` to opt out of caller isolation
- Good candidates: weather API fetch methods, trigger evaluation logic

---

## Phase 5: Xcode 26.4 Testing Improvements

### 5.1 — Adopt image attachments in Swift Testing
Xcode 26.4 supports attaching `UIImage`/`CGImage` directly to test results:
- Consider adding snapshot/image-based test attachments for weather UI components
- This is optional but useful for visual regression testing

### 5.2 — Adopt severity levels for test issues
- Use the new severity level API to differentiate warnings vs. critical test failures
- Apply to existing tests where appropriate

---

## Phase 6: Verify & Build

### 6.1 — Build the project
- Run full build with `xcodebuild -scheme SunHat -configuration Debug -destination 'generic/platform=iOS Simulator' build`
- Fix any Swift 6.2 compiler warnings or errors from behavioral changes

### 6.2 — Run tests
- Verify all existing tests pass with the new deployment target and Swift version

### 6.3 — Update documentation
- Update iOS-26-Migration-Guide.md with 26.4 changes
- Update CLAUDE.md references

---

